<blockquote>
<p>1. The article is not thematically in line with the Foundation. There is too much emphasis on the suffering and misery of the SCP, how she's suicidal and all that jazz, and very little emphasis on the anomalous properties. Unless her anomalous property is that she's constantly miserable and depressed.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>''Protect'' is also a part of the Foundation mantra, that includes the SCP itself. Besides not being sure what happens if she does die, I tried to make sure that all information about her psychological state is adding to properly securing it better. Think about it: If you're containment personnel, you need to be aware of her suicidal tendencies because it would be too much of a risk if you're caught by surprise.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>2. The SCP has next to no personality. Even with interview logs and stuff, there isn't much to her other than &quot;constantly miserable&quot;, which IMO, is not realistic. Even when people are severely depressed, they still retain at least a few of their individual personality quirks.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I agree about the personality, but keep in mind that the format of an article like this only allows characterization from the perspective of the Foundation itself, AKA interview logs and the notes at the end. The Foundation considers the risk of suicide important, but her hobbies aren't something the security document on an SCP needs to have. Elaborating on personality outside of that would be weird in-universe.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>3. My biggest gripe: the SCP is too melodramatic to be realistic. There's too much emphasis on her torment and too many terrible things happen to her without rhyme or reason. All in all it feels more like a clumsy attempt at &quot;She is SUFFERING! Feel bad for her!&quot; rather than a genuine tragedy. I can't feel sorry for her because the sheer misfortune she has gone through is just too over-the-top and it destroys my suspension of disbelief.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Well&#8230;you're certainly direct about that. That's fair.</p>

